  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/668d0aff-b1d3-45c8-bcbe-29005000d645-image.png\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 250px;\" /><br /><br />Equation of tangent at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is &nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Equation of normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Here tangent and normal passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Equation of tangent is <math><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></math><br /><br />Equation of normal is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math><br /><br />Tangent and normal intersect x-axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />Since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a right angled triangle, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is the diameter for the circle.</p><p>Also mid point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is center&nbsp;of the circle.<br /><br />Hence Centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />Slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></math><math><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
